C     Common block for the names for gates.  Includes the
C     information needed to place the flow class and the current 
C     gate opening in the special output file.  Start the GOPEN and
C     FCLASS at 0 to provide space for gates/pumps without a name.
C     We can then avoid an IF statement to see if we should store
C     something.  If no name is given the data goes into slot
C     zero and is never used!  FCLASS_CODE gives a unique numerical
C     code for each flow class string given in FCLASS.

C     Use slot MNGATE+1 for the McHenry gates.

      INTEGER NGATE

      REAL GOPEN(0:MNGATE+1)

      INTEGER FCLASS_CODE(0:MNGATE+1)

      CHARACTER GNAME(MNGATE+1)*16, FCLASS(0:MNGATE+1)*8


C     FCLASS gives the flow class of the gate.  The meaning of this field 
C     depends on the gate type and the kinds of flow that FEQ can report.

      COMMON/GATE1/ NGATE, GOPEN, FCLASS_CODE
      COMMON/GATE2/ GNAME, FCLASS

      SAVE /GATE1/, /GATE2/
    
